"Start hidden": a child webview created with its native view hidden.

Applies to: tauri-runtime-cef 3.0.0-alpha.7 (crates.io) + 0001, 0003, 0004, 0005, applied in
vendor/tauri-runtime-cef. Not offered upstream yet; `WebviewBuilderCefExt::start_hidden` is
the shape it would take.

Why: a child webview is added to its window visible, with an opaque white background, and
Tauri has no attribute to create it hidden. Eos makes its artifact, browser, preview and
other-computer views off screen and hides them right after `add_child`, but the window draws
the new view before that hide arrives: a white rectangle flashes over the dashboard each
time one is made. With `start_hidden()` the view is created with CEF's `hidden` window info
and its NSView is hidden in the same main-thread turn as the creation, so it is never drawn;
`Webview::show` brings it up as before.

